<title>PORTUGAL: BPI sets ratio for capital call.</title>
<headline>BPI sets ratio for capital call.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Portugues de Investimento's 30 billion escudo capital call will be made on the basis of one new share for every 2.6 shares held, a bank spokesman said.</p>
<p>Earlier, the bank had announced that the offer would be priced at 1,400 escudos per share but gave no further details in a statement.</p>
<p>The capital call is to pay for its purchase of Banco de Fomento &amp; Exterior. The bank said that the call was expected to be launched in the second half of November.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bourse 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
